  "worked_solution": "Let's recall the graph of $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14254255/assets/7808808bd051a8a291fb9639b0a042d9af2e50bbecb0ccaf65b7885ac792b68a.png)\n\nThe function has a maximum at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ and the period of the function is $2\\pi .$ Therefore, the maximum values of the function occur at:\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi \n$$",
